@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option desk - Provider resolution by capability, never by vendor

component "A command needs a capability:\noption_chain | underlying_quote |\nrisk_free_rate | underlying_history |\ndividend_yield" as need
component "Registry\npriority order,\nkeyless providers always eligible,\nkeyed providers skipped\nwhen the key is absent" as reg #C6E9C6
component "Alpha Vantage\nkey required\nhistory and quotes\n~25 requests/day free tier" as paid
component "Yahoo\nfree, delayed,\nall capabilities" as yahoo
component "ProviderUnavailable\nnames every candidate\nand why each was skipped" as err
component "Artifact records provider_used\nin the meta block" as art

need --> reg
reg --> paid : key present
reg --> yahoo : always available
reg --> err : nothing can answer
paid --> art
yahoo --> art

note right of reg
--provider is strict: if the named
provider cannot answer, the command
fails rather than quietly serving a
different source. strict=False in code
allows the fallback.
end note

note bottom of art
Keys resolve from CLI flag, then
environment, then ./.env, then
~/.optiondesk/config.env. They are
read, never written to artifacts,
never logged, prompted with
hidden input.
end note

note bottom of yahoo
A licence on this software grants
no rights over the data it retrieves:
each provider's terms govern that.
end note

caption Adding a provider is a class plus one line of priority: it is selected when its key is present and skipped when it is not.
@enduml
